        "claim": "Three blended weights and a light-society-nature index score New York, Bellevue, Sedona, and Yellowstone at 35.55, 41.33, 76.94, and 84.18; of the three strategies at an equal ten percent dose, cutting artificial light lifts the index most in both the city and the countryside, though New York stays in the worst grade.",
